WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:20.829
"Roger Redbeard was hanging around outside your house?" Henry asked William. "Why?"

2
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:25.742
"I don't know. I only saw him for a second." William looked around.

3
00:00:25.743 --> 00:00:28.347
"Hey, where's everybody else?"

4
00:00:28.348 --> 00:00:31.318
"I think they're over there." Cole pointed.

5
00:00:31.319 --> 00:00:36.080
William took a few steps and then paused. "Aren't you guys coming?"

6
00:00:36.081 --> 00:00:39.179
"We'll be there in a minute," Henry said.

7
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.807
After William left, Cole shrugged. "That's weird," he said.

8
00:00:43.808 --> 00:00:48.806
"Why is Roger hanging around William's house? Is he looking for more booty?"

9
00:00:48.807 --> 00:00:54.159
"Maybe." Henry glanced at the general store.

10
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.952
"Come on, let's go inside and ask if Roger was really here earlier.

11
00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:05.687
Maybe he found that cup on the beach and used it for his alibi."

12
00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:08.577
Henry and Cole hurried into the general store.

13
00:01:08.578 --> 00:01:11.339
A woman was behind the cash register.

14
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.034
She had a friendly smile and hair the same color as Anna's.

15
00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:21.218
"Hello, boys," she greeted them. "I haven't seen you around here before.

16
00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:24.101
Are you William's new friends from Belltown?"

17
00:01:24.102 --> 00:01:27.072
Henry guessed that the woman was Anna's mother.

18
00:01:27.073 --> 00:01:30.337
He also guessed that Anna had told her about their visit.

19
00:01:30.338 --> 00:01:33.029
"Yes, we are," he told her.

20
00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.809
"Welcome to Sea Cove," Anna's mother said.

21
00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.447
"I hope you're enjoying the treasure hunt."

22
00:01:39.448 --> 00:01:41.978
"It's great," Cole said.

23
00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:45.381
"We were wondering something," Henry added.

24
00:01:45.382 --> 00:01:50.085
"Did a man named Roger Redbeard come in here a little while ago?"

25
00:01:50.086 --> 00:01:57.595
"Roger?" Anna's mom smiled. "Why yes. He did come in earlier today."

26
00:01:57.596 --> 00:02:00.832
Just then another customer came toward the register.

27
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:04.844
Henry and Cole stepped away to talk.

28
00:02:04.845 --> 00:02:09.135
"I guess Roger does have a good alibi after all," Cole said.

29
00:02:09.136 --> 00:02:12.609
"If he was here earlier, he couldn't have taken those tickets."

30
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.772
"Yeah." Henry bit his lip.

31
00:02:15.773 --> 00:02:22.295
If Roger hadn't done it, that meant one of their friends was the thief. "Let's go."

32
00:02:22.296 --> 00:02:25.463
"Hold on." Cole stepped toward a shelf.

33
00:02:25.464 --> 00:02:29.932
"Seeing that gum earlier made me want some. I think I'll buy some now."

34
00:02:29.933 --> 00:02:35.158
He grabbed a pack of cherry gum from the shelf.

35
00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:38.573
Henry and Cole waited for the other customer to finish.

36
00:02:38.574 --> 00:02:40.886
Then they stepped up to the counter again.

37
00:02:40.887 --> 00:02:44.030
Cole set down his pack of cherry gum.

38
00:02:44.031 --> 00:02:48.958
"Do you need anything else, boys?" Anna's mom asked as she rang up the sale.

39
00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:52.867
Cole handed over a dollar. "No, thanks."

40
00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:59.468
Henry was staring at the gum, still thinking about what William had just told them about seeing Roger again.

41
00:02:59.469 --> 00:03:03.313
Something didn't seem quite right about Roger's story.

42
00:03:03.314 --> 00:03:06.083
Why did they keep seeing him everywhere?

43
00:03:06.084 --> 00:03:11.589
"Excuse me," Henry said to Anna's mom. "Is Anna's sister around?"

44
00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:16.887
If Roger had really seen Anna's sister on the beach, maybe she'd seen him too.

45
00:03:16.888 --> 00:03:21.466
Or maybe she'd seen something else suspicious while she was out jogging.

46
00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:26.538
Anna's mom looked surprised. "Do you mean Josie?" she said.

47
00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.255
"She's not here right now.

48
00:03:28.256 --> 00:03:31.907
She's spending the whole weekend with friends out of town."

49
00:03:31.908 --> 00:03:36.552
"Really?" Henry said. "Is that Anna's only sister?"

50
00:03:36.553 --> 00:03:39.162
Anna's mom laughed.

51
00:03:39.163 --> 00:03:45.594
"Yes. And trust me, two kids in one family is plenty!" she said with a wink.

52
00:03:45.595 --> 00:03:52.060
"Okay, thanks." Henry wandered toward the door along with Cole, still thinking hard.

53
00:03:52.061 --> 00:03:55.584
Had Roger lied about seeing "the Jones girl" on the beach?

54
00:03:55.585 --> 00:03:57.908
Or was something else going on?

55
00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:02.202
He kept thinking as he and Cole left the general store.

56
00:04:02.203 --> 00:04:05.377
"We'd better find the others," Cole said.

57
00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:11.353
"Uh-huh." Henry didn't say anything else.

58
00:04:11.354 --> 00:04:15.749
He just kept thinking as he followed Cole across the street.

59
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:21.518
He thought about everything that had happened so far, and everything everyone had said all day.

60
00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:27.847
Someone was lying. And Henry was starting to figure out who it might be . . .

61
00:04:27.848 --> 00:04:32.853
Cole and Henry found the others standing at the edge of a small but pretty park.

62
00:04:32.854 --> 00:04:37.475
"We've been looking all over for you!" Maggie cried when she spotted them.

63
00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:41.842
"Yeah," Luke added. "We think we know where the next booty is hidden."

64
00:04:41.843 --> 00:04:43.767
Maggie nodded and pointed.

65
00:04:43.768 --> 00:04:47.431
"We're pretty sure it's in the old bandstand over there."

66
00:04:47.432 --> 00:04:51.968
"What are we waiting for?" Cole exclaimed. "Let's go!"

67
00:04:51.969 --> 00:04:55.388
"Wait," Henry spoke up before they could rush off.

68
00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:58.638
"First I need to ask Luke something.

69
00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:04.087
Remember when you and Nathan found the treasure in the tide pool and were waiting for the rest of us?"

70
00:05:04.088 --> 00:05:08.019
"Yeah," Luke said. "So?"

71
00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:13.081
"So exactly when did William get there?" Henry asked.

72
00:05:13.082 --> 00:05:18.403
William frowned. "I just told you guys I didn't take those tickets!" he cried.

73
00:05:18.404 --> 00:05:20.512
"I thought you believed me!"

74
00:05:20.513 --> 00:05:24.363
"Don't worry, I do believe you," Henry assured him.

75
00:05:24.364 --> 00:05:27.835
He continued to look at Luke. "Well?"

76
00:05:27.836 --> 00:05:34.037
Luke shrugged. "Actually, William was already there when Nathan and I found the tide pool."

77
00:05:34.038 --> 00:05:36.931
Nathan nodded. "Yeah."

78
00:05:36.932 --> 00:05:40.305
"Do you have a theory, Henry?" Maggie demanded.

79
00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:44.695
"Did William steal those tickets? Or was it Nathan and Luke?"

80
00:05:44.696 --> 00:05:57.750
"No, it wasn't any of them," Henry replied. "It was Anna."
